-- title:
--   Cyclotomic extension of a complete unramified DVR
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and let $W_0$ be a commutative domain which is a discrete valuation ring, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, and whose maximal ideal is the principal ideal generated by the image of $q$. Let $k$ be a field of characteristic $q$ and let $\mathrm{res}_0 \colon W_0 \to k$ be a surjective ring homomorphism whose kernel is the maximal ideal of $W_0$, so that $k$ is identified with the residue field. The assertion is the existence of a type $\mathcal{O}$ carrying a commutative ring structure making it a domain and a discrete valuation ring, together with a $W_0$-algebra structure and adic completeness for its own maximal ideal, an element $\zeta \in \mathcal{O}$ and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{res} \colon \mathcal{O} \to k$, such that: $\sum_{i<q} \zeta^i = 0$; the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}$ is generated by $\zeta - 1$; $\mathrm{res}$ is surjective with kernel the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}$; $\mathrm{res}(\mathrm{algebraMap}\,w) = \mathrm{res}_0(w)$ for all $w \in W_0$; and for every commutative $W_0$-algebra $S$ and every $z \in S$ with $\sum_{i<q} z^i = 0$ there is exactly one $W_0$-algebra homomorphism $\mathcal{O} \to S$ carrying $\zeta$ to $z$.
--
--   This is the construction of the totally ramified cyclotomic extension $W_0[\zeta_q]$ of a complete unramified discrete valuation ring of residue characteristic $q$: the uniformiser is $\zeta - 1$, the residue field is unchanged, and the final clause records that $\mathcal{O}$ is, up to unique isomorphism, $W_0[X]/(1 + X + \dots + X^{q-1})$. It serves as a coefficient-ring construction and is cited by [`IsPrimitiveRoot.exists_isDiscreteValuationRing_isAdicComplete_ringHom_comp_eq_maximalIdeal_eq_span_pow_sub_one_eq_mul_of_adjoin_eq_top`](thm.html#IsPrimitiveRoot.exists_isDiscreteValuationRing_isAdicComplete_ringHom_comp_eq_maximalIdeal_eq_span_pow_sub_one_eq_mul_of_adjoin_eq_top).
